  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our best result (config_016, 52.7% acc) is multimodal with singleprofile, PCA-2000, ResNet50, and concat fusion. The image modality alone is very weak (20.8%), so the ~4.2% multimodal gain is modest. Critically, we have zero evidence on whether multiprofile helps, which is a foundational design choice for cellular profiling. Question: Does aggregating multiple profiles per cell (via avgpool) improve over singleprofile, holding all other variables constant? Why this is the best next experiment: config_018 is the minimal logical extension of our current best (config_016) — it changes only profile_setting (single→multi) and adds the necessary aggregation (avgpool), keeping RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion identical. This isolates the multiprofile effect cleanly. If multiprofile helps, it reshapes the entire remaining search (all subsequent multimodal configs should use multiprofile); if it doesn't, we can focus budget on encoder/fusion variations. Under limited budget, resolving this binary design question has the highest information value per experiment."
}

